# GitHub Account: jrrqd

This workspace is bound to the **`jrrqd`** GitHub account. Treat any other GitHub identity as wrong for this project.

## Authoritative source

The active GitHub CLI identity is stored in `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml` under `user:`. That file is the source of truth — read it before any GitHub-scoped work and assume `jrrqd` unless it says otherwise.

## Commit author

- `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` for this repo must resolve to the `jrrqd` GitHub account.
- If they don't, ask before changing them. Do not silently rewrite commit history.

## Remote URLs

- Prefer SSH remotes under `git@github.com:jrrqd/...`.
- Do not push, open PRs against, or interact with repos owned by other users/Orgs unless the user explicitly asks for it in that turn.

## GitHub CLI (`gh`)

- The `gh` binary is not on `$PATH` by default; it lives at `/tmp/gh_2.96.0_macOS_arm64/bin/gh`. Use that full path, or ask the user before adding it to a shell rc.
- Before any `gh` call that touches GitHub (auth status, issue/PR create, repo view, etc.), confirm the active user with `gh auth status` and stop if it is not `jrrqd`.

## When the user asks to "switch GitHub account"

1. Edit `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml` and change `user:` to the requested account. Do not delete other remembered users under `users:` — keep them so switching back is reversible.
2. If the request implies changing commit author too, also update local git config — but ask first; never rewrite past commits.
